# Engenty naming (not “specialist”)

Hired custom agents in a space are **Engenties**. Never call them specialists in UI copy, empty states, wizards, agent instructions, or people-facing docs.

| | Use |
|---|---|
| One | **Engenty** (`an Engenty`) |
| Many | **engenties** |
| Section chrome | Agents (the list heading can stay) |
| Internal role id | `specialist` on the registry row — do not rename the enum |

```text
❌ Hire a specialist / name the specialist / Engenty specialist
✅ Hire an Engenty / name the Engenty / You are an Engenty in this space
```

`role: "specialist"` in code is the classification (vs copilot, coordinator, delegated). It is not a word a person should read.
